{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require jury trials for all civil litigation claims exceeding \u00a31 billion",
        "additional_details": "Prior to 1933, civil jury trials were common in England. Recently multi-billion pound mass-tort litigations have been put to a single judge to make the final court decision. We believe such massive public-interest decisions should not rest on one individual. \r\n \r\nRestoring juries for civil claims could help ensure democratic transparency, and community alignment in the UK's highest-stakes corporate legal battles.",
        "background": "Mandate the use of jury trials for all civil litigation claims exceeding \u00a31 billion.",
